# Scratch API responses left in the repo root by an agent session. Nothing
# reads them. Ignored because several sessions share this checkout: such a file
# turned up staged once already, and a `git add -A` from any of them would
# commit it.
#
# #318 listed one name, nr.json (an ArcGIS municipality query from the #298
# work). Four more had appeared by 2026-08-26 — portal_home.html, q_candin1.json,
# q_candin2.json, wms_test.xml (Wikidata entities and an ArcGIS error page) —
# so this closes the class instead of the examples: the root holds no tracked
# .json, .html or .xml at all, only .py, .md, .yml, .toml and dotfiles. A file
# of those types in the root is a dump by definition. Add a negation below if
# that ever stops being true.
/*.json
/*.html
/*.xml
# data/ holds runtime artifacts (backfill snapshots, call ledgers) that must
# never be committed — but the four REFERENCE files below are reviewed, small,
# and deploy with the code: the QoL card and /municipalities read three of them
# (regenerate via utils/import_ine_data.py, utils/import_cnh_hospitals.py and
# utils/import_sepe_unemployment.py), and /agencies reads top_agencies.json,
# which has no importer at all — it is measured and edited by hand.
# `data/*` rather than `data/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# *directory* is excluded, so the bare-directory form made the negations
# silently dead.
data/*
!data/ine_municipal.json
!data/hospitals_cnh.json
!data/sepe_unemployment.json
!data/top_agencies.json
instance/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

