# Full-source distribution bundles (issue #29: served unauthenticated from
# static/, which Flask serves directly regardless of any route decorator —
# never let these get committed again)
static/idealista-project*.zip
static/idealista-project*.tar.gz
static/all_code.txt

# Archives anywhere in the tree. The three blobs from #29 stayed reachable in
# git history long after the live route was gone, so the guard is a blanket
# one now. A genuinely needed fixture can be added with `git add -f`.
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
.mcp.json
.worktrees/
.kimi-code/mcp.json
# Wrangler's cache, which this project never asked for: there is no wrangler
# config anywhere in the tree. It appears because `wrangler` writes
# `.wrangler/` into whatever directory it is run from, and this machine has ten
# of them across the owner's other sites — so any session that ever runs it
# with this checkout as its cwd leaves one here, with nobody at fault.
#
# Ignored rather than tidied away by hand, because 54 bytes of it disabled the
# Tier 2 final gate for every session at once on 2026-08-27: the gate refuses
# *every* action — tests, review, consume — on a worktree that is not clean
# including untracked files, and answers `target repository worktree is not
# clean` with no hint as to which file it means.
#
# It has to be here rather than in the machine's `~/.config/git/ignore`, and
# that was measured after the global rule was tried first and did not work.
# `final_gate.py:_git` runs git with `env={"PATH": ..., "LANG": "C", "LC_ALL":
# "C"}` and deliberately no `HOME`, so a global ignore is invisible to it —
# the same isolation that stops anyone feeding the gate rules from outside.
# A repository `.gitignore` needs no `HOME` and is therefore the only form
# that works.
.wrangler/
